        </div>
      </div>

      <div class='tip-card'>
        <div class='tip-number'>3</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Strings vs Values</h3>
          <p>The string <code>"0"</code> is truthy (non-empty string). The number <code>0</code> is falsy. Watch out for this common confusion!</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class='tip-card'>
        <div class='tip-number'>4</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Use It for Checking Variables</h3>
          <p>Instead of <code>if (name !== "")</code>, you can write <code>if (name)</code>. JavaScript's truthiness makes your code cleaner!</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
